    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Piecewise linear integrand",
        "body": "The integrand $f$ is even, so compute $\\int_0^{10}f$ and double it. For $x\\ge0$ the nested absolute values change slope only where an inner expression vanishes: $x=1$, $x=3$, $x=6$ and $x=10$. The values are $f(0)=2$, $f(1)=3$, $f(3)=1$, $f(6)=4$, $f(10)=0$, and $f$ is linear in between.\n\nAreas of the trapezoids: $[0,1]$: $\\frac{2+3}2=2.5$; $[1,3]$: $\\frac{3+1}2\\cdot2=4$; $[3,6]$: $\\frac{1+4}2\\cdot3=7.5$; $[6,10]$: $\\frac{4+0}2\\cdot4=8$. Total $\\int_0^{10}f=22$, so the integral is $44$.\n\n**Answer: 44**"
      }
