        "title": "Product to sum",
        "body": "$\\sin A\\cos B=\\frac12[\\sin(A+B)+\\sin(A-B)]$ with $A=\\frac\\pi{12}+x$, $B=\\frac\\pi{12}-x$ gives $\\frac12\\left[\\sin\\frac\\pi6+\\sin2x\\right]=\\frac14+\\frac12\\sin2x$.\n\nThe term $x^{2022}\\sin 2x$ is odd, so it integrates to $0$ over $[-1,1]$. Remaining: $\\frac14\\int_{-1}^1x^{2022}dx=\\frac14\\cdot\\frac2{2023}=\\frac1{4046}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac1{4046}$**"
