    "answer": "pi*ln(3)^3/48",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Symmetry $x\\to1/x$",
        "body": "Let $I$ be the integral. Substituting $x\\to\\frac1x$ maps the interval to itself, keeps $\\frac{dx}x$ (up to orientation) and $\\log^2x$, and turns $\\arctan x$ into $\\arctan\\frac1x=\\frac\\pi2-\\arctan x$. Hence $I=\\int\\left(\\frac\\pi2-\\arctan x\\right)\\frac{\\log^2x}{x}dx$ and adding the two expressions, $$2I=\\frac\\pi2\\int_{1/\\sqrt3}^{\\sqrt3}\\frac{\\log^2x}x\\,dx=\\frac\\pi2\\left[\\frac{\\log^3x}3\\right]_{1/\\sqrt3}^{\\sqrt3}=\\frac\\pi2\\cdot\\frac23\\left(\\frac{\\log3}2\\right)^3=\\frac{\\pi\\log^33}{24}.$$ So $I=\\frac{\\pi\\log^33}{48}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{\\pi}{48}\\log^33$**"
      }
    ],
